---
title: "Visually Hidden"
description: "Hides content visually while keeping it available to screen readers."
tags: [accessibility, utility, css]
usage: |
  Add the `visually-hidden` class to text that should be read but not seen, such
  as the label of an icon-only button or extra context for a link.
accessibility: |
  - The content becomes visible while it has focus, so it also works for skip
    links.
  - Do not use it to hide content from everyone: use `hidden` for that.
  - When the visible content is decorative, hide it with `aria-hidden="true"` so
    it is not read twice.
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<button type="button">
  <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
  <span class="visually-hidden">Close dialog</span>
</button>
